# DW modeling

Gold is a bottom-up Kimball mart (fact constellation). Layer placement is in `05-medallion-layers`. This file is the modeling contract.

## Grain comment

The first comment on every fact DDL or load function states the grain in one sentence.

```sql
-- grain: one row = one order item (order_id, order_item_id)
CREATE TABLE {gold}.fact_order_item ( ... );
```

Locked grains (do not change without SPEC §10):

- `fact_order_item`: one item of one order (`order_id`, `order_item_id`). Transaction fact.
- `fact_order`: one order. Accumulating snapshot.
- `fact_seller_monthly`: one seller × one active month. Periodic snapshot.

## Keys and dimensions

- Every dimension has a surrogate key. Business keys (`seller_id`, `customer_unique_id`, …) stay as attributes.
- Member `-1` means Unknown on every dimension. Do not drop late-arriving FKs; point them at `-1` and count them in `gold.etl_audit`.
- Dimensions are conformed across the three facts. `dim_date` is role-playing (purchase, approved, shipping limit, delivered to carrier, delivered to customer, estimated). `dim_month` is the shrunken month dimension.
- `dim_customer` is keyed by `customer_unique_id`. Map per-order `customer_id` in Silver.
- SCD Type 2 on `dim_seller` is bonus (R41), not required. If you add it, include `effective_from`, `effective_to`, and `is_current`, and say so in DESIGN §2.

## Measures

- Additive (sum in OLAP): `price`, `freight_value`, `items_value`, `freight_total`, `payment_total`, counts, 0/1 flags.
- Non-additive (average or percentile only): `delivery_days`, `delay_days`, `seller_handling_days`, `review_score`, `distance_km`, and any `*_rate`.
- Do not `SUM` a rate column. Recompute rates from additive numerators and denominators.

## DESIGN stays in sync

A schema change in the same session updates DESIGN §6 (source-to-target) and §8 (data dictionary). Leave sections marked `_chưa điền_` empty until you have a real mapping; do not invent columns. Bus-matrix ticks in DESIGN §2 already match SPEC; change them only when SPEC changes.
